Complete the compiler-version policy for the Adreno OpenCL workarounds and make
the whole family reachable for field isolation.

The comments in this file already say the q6_K flat GEMV miscompile and the FA
clBuildProgram crash are defects of older E031 compilers, not of a GPU generation.
Three gates still looked at the generation only, which left the A6X and the models
the generation table does not know with no protection at all. The version-string
parsing and the OPFILTER regex could also throw during backend init, and no runtime
key could switch the Adreno kernel family off.

- gate the lm_head CPU bypass, the flat-GEMV size escape and the two FA mixed/
  quant-KV declines on q6_k_flat_old_compiler as well (widening only)
- parse the compiler version without std::out_of_range; a missing field reads as
  -1 ("older than any threshold"); a bad OPFILTER pattern no longer escapes into
  std::terminate
- add GGML_OPENCL_ADRENO_KERNELS / GGML_OPENCL_Q40_KERNELS / GGML_OPENCL_Q6K_KERNELS
  off switches inside use_adreno_kernels()

The matching llama.rn-side channel ("_oclEnv" in llamaInitContext) is in
cpp/jsi/RNLlamaJSI.cpp.

